### Additional context

Related to #69619

`tsc --lsp` registers formatting, range formatting and on-type formatting for every content-mapped extension. A mapper can only turn off formatting edits per span (the `Formatting` span feature), not the registrations. When the mapped language has its own formatter, editors then offer TypeScript 7 as a formatter for those files, and choosing it does nothing.

### Use case

TSRX (`.tsrx`) files are formatted by Prettier with `@tsrx/prettier-plugin`, and the TSRX language server serves that as `textDocument/formatting` in every editor. TypeScript cannot format a `.tsrx` file, because the generated TSX is not the source. So the TSRX mapper sets no `Formatting` feature on any span, and TypeScript 7 returns no edits:

```
App.tsrx  textDocument/formatting       → []
App.tsrx  textDocument/rangeFormatting  → []
```

`tsc --lsp` still registers all three for `**/*.tsrx`, so:

- VS Code lists TypeScript 7 in **Format Document With…** for `.tsrx` files, with an entry that does nothing. The TSRX extension sets itself as the `[tsrx]` default formatter to keep **Format Document** working.
- An editor that runs `tsc --lsp` next to the TSRX language server can choose TypeScript 7 for a `.tsrx` file and format nothing.

### What tsc --lsp registers

With the identity mapper from https://gist.github.com/leonidaz/d1fcd2d140269282c7df1d3b84fe517f (`.foo` files contain TSX, one verbatim span with all features), `ask-formatting.mjs` (below) shows, on `7.1.0-dev.20260930.4`:

```
content-mapper-formatting (textDocument/formatting) [{"pattern":"**/*.foo"}]
content-mapper-range-formatting (textDocument/rangeFormatting) [{"pattern":"**/*.foo"}]
content-mapper-on-type-formatting (textDocument/onTypeFormatting) [{"pattern":"**/*.foo"}]
```

For this mapper the registrations are correct: `main.foo` gets the same formatting edits as the same text in `control.ts`. The server makes them for every mapped extension ([server.go#L650-L670](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/15dee00a1c6549a4953ab17ccac4c56d252ba4cc/tsc/internal/lsp/server.go#L650-L670)), and a mapper has no way to say that its files have no TypeScript formatting.

### Suggestion

Let a mapper declare that TypeScript should not format its files, for example with a field in the mapper's `initialize` result or in its package's `typescript.contentMapper` entry. For that mapper's extensions, the server then skips the three formatting registrations. A mapper that declares nothing keeps today's behavior.

Found while adding TypeScript 7 support for `.tsrx` files (https://github.com/tsrx-org/tsrx/issues/136).

<details>
<summary><code>ask-formatting.mjs</code>: put it next to the gist's files, run <code>npm install --ignore-scripts</code>, <code>npm run setup</code>, then <code>node ask-formatting.mjs</code> (it rewrites <code>main.foo</code> and <code>control.ts</code>)</summary>

```js
// Records which formatting features `tsc --lsp` registers for content-mapped
// files, and what they return for main.foo and control.ts (same messy text).
import { spawn } from "node:child_process";
import { writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from "node:url";

const root = fileURLToPath(new URL(".", import.meta.url));
const messy = 'import { greet } from "greeting";\nexport const text   =greet( "x" )\n';
writeFileSync(`${root}main.foo`, messy);
writeFileSync(`${root}control.ts`, messy);
const tsc = fileURLToPath(new URL("./node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc", import.meta.url));
const server = spawn(process.execPath, [tsc, "--lsp", "--stdio"], { cwd: root, stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "inherit"] });

let nextId = 1;
const pending = new Map();
const registrations = [];
let buffered = Buffer.alloc(0);
const send = (message) => {
  const body = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: "2.0", ...message }));
  server.stdin.write(`Content-Length: ${body.length}\r\n\r\n`);
  server.stdin.write(body);
};
const request = (method, params) => new Promise((resolve) => { const id = nextId++; pending.set(id, resolve); send({ id, method, params }); });
server.stdout.on("data", (chunk) => {
  buffered = Buffer.concat([buffered, chunk]);
  while (true) {
    const headerEnd = buffered.indexOf("\r\n\r\n");
    if (headerEnd < 0) return;
    const length = Number(/Content-Length: (\d+)/i.exec(buffered.subarray(0, headerEnd).toString())[1]);
    if (buffered.length < headerEnd + 4 + length) return;
    const message = JSON.parse(buffered.subarray(headerEnd + 4, headerEnd + 4 + length).toString());
    buffered = buffered.subarray(headerEnd + 4 + length);
    if (message.method && message.id !== undefined) {
      if (message.method === "client/registerCapability") registrations.push(...message.params.registrations);
      const result = message.method === "workspace/configuration" ? message.params.items.map(() => null) : null;
      send({ id: message.id, result });
    } else if (message.id !== undefined && pending.has(message.id)) {
      pending.get(message.id)(message.result ?? message.error);
      pending.delete(message.id);
    }
  }
});
const uri = (file) => pathToFileURL(`${root}${file}`).href;
await request("initialize", {
  processId: process.pid,
  rootUri: pathToFileURL(root).href,
  workspaceFolders: [{ uri: pathToFileURL(root).href, name: "repro" }],
  capabilities: {
    workspace: { configuration: true, workspaceFolders: true },
    textDocument: {
      synchronization: { dynamicRegistration: true },
      diagnostic: { dynamicRegistration: true },
      formatting: { dynamicRegistration: true },
      rangeFormatting: { dynamicRegistration: true },
      onTypeFormatting: { dynamicRegistration: true },
    },
  },
  initializationOptions: { runExternalCode: true },
});
send({ method: "initialized", params: {} });
const options = { tabSize: 2, insertSpaces: true };
for (const [file, languageId] of [["main.foo", "plaintext"], ["control.ts", "typescript"]]) {
  send({ method: "textDocument/didOpen", params: { textDocument: { uri: uri(file), languageId, version: 1, text: messy } } });
  await request("textDocument/diagnostic", { textDocument: { uri: uri(file) } });
  const formatting = await request("textDocument/formatting", { textDocument: { uri: uri(file) }, options });
  console.log(`${file} formatting: ${JSON.stringify(formatting)}`);
}
console.log("content-mapper registrations:");
for (const r of registrations.filter((r) => /format/i.test(r.id))) console.log(`  ${r.id} (${r.method}) ${JSON.stringify(r.registerOptions?.documentSelector)}`);
await request("shutdown");
send({ method: "exit" });
```

