### Problem Description

When `index.mapping.exclude_source_vectors` is explicitly set to `false` on an index with an indexed `dense_vector` field, the field's vectors are read from the stored `_source` rather than being decoded from doc values. For `element_type: byte` or `element_type: bit` fields, users may index vectors as hex or base64 strings (e.g. `"textvector": "0BB8"`). In this case the `diversify` retriever silently drops every document from diversification, effectively returning results as if no vectors were present.

### Steps to Reproduce

```json
PUT /test-byte-vec-index
{
  "settings": { "index.mapping.exclude_source_vectors": false },
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "textvector": { "type": "dense_vector", "dims": 16, "element_type": "bit" }
    }
  }
}

POST /test-byte-vec-index/_bulk?refresh=true
{"index":{}}
{"id": 1, "textvector": "0BB8"}
{"index":{}}
{"id": 2, "textvector": "94A2"}
{"index":{}}
{"id": 3, "textvector": "0560"}
{"index":{}}
{"id": 4, "textvector": "2112"}
{"index":{}}
{"id": 5, "textvector": "5051"}

GET /test-byte-vec-index/_search
{
  "retriever": {
    "diversify": {
      "type": "mmr",
      "field": "textvector",
      "size": 3,
      "lambda": 0.7,
      "retriever": { "standard": { "query": { "match_all": {} } } }
    }
  }
}
```

**Expected:** 3 diversified results selected by MMR using the actual bit vectors.

**Actual:** 0 hits returned — all documents are silently dropped from diversification.

